description:
Design a buffered output driver with sleep mode functionality. The module outputs the signal A to the output X when SLEEP is inactive (i.e., SLEEP=0); otherwise, when SLEEP is active (SLEEP=1), the output X is driven LOW, effectively disabling the output. This functionality serves to conserve power by turning off the output when the device is in sleep mode.
module top_module(
    X    ,
    SLEEP,
    A
);

