description:
Design a sequential circuit that operates on a clock signal. The output, q, is updated on the rising edge of the clock based on the input signal a. If a is high, the next state of q (q_next) is set to LOW; otherwise, it is set to HIGH. This effectively creates a toggle behavior for the output q, making it a simple state machine that flips its state based on the input condition, providing an inversion on each clock cycle when the input a is LOW.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input a,
  output reg q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input a,
  output reg q
);reg q_next;

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    q <= q_next;
  end

  always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (a) begin
      q_next <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      q_next <= 1'b1;
    end
  end

endmodule

