Implement an 8-bit ripple carry adder that computes the sum of two 8-bit inputs, `in1` and `in2`, producing a 9-bit output `res` to accommodate potential overflow. This module employs a series of XOR gates to generate sum bits and AND-OR combinations to produce carry bits sequentially, allowing the calculated carry from each bit addition to propagate to the next higher bit. The overall design efficiently combines combinational logic to achieve binary addition while ensuring accurate handling of carry propagation for each pair of bits.
